\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 Cleaning Steps\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 Step 1: Compute 12-Month-Ending ODD Liver Transplant Counts\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Using the monthly ODD liver transplant counts from Figure 4 (SPSS crosstab output), compute a rolling 12-month sum in Excel for each month from August 2023 through December 2024.\
For example, the 12-month-ending count for August 2023 = sum of monthly ODD liver transplants from September 2022 through August 2023.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 Step 2: Compute 12-Month-Ending Overdose Death Counts\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Extract predicted provisional death counts from the CDC NCHS database for each month from August 2023 through December 2024. These are already provided as 12-month-ending counts by CDC.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 Step 3: Assign Mid-Window Population\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 For each 12-month window, assign the US resident population at the approximate midpoint of the window.\
For example, for the 12-month window ending August 2023 (September 2022\'96August 2023), use the March 1, 2023 resident population estimate. For the window ending March 2024 (April 2023\'96March 2024), use the October 1, 2023 estimate. For the window ending December 2024 (January 2024\'96December 2024), use the July 1, 2024 estimate.\
Population source assignment follows Figure 1: Census 2010-series through December 2020, Census 2020-series from January 2021 onward.\
The same mid-window population is used as the denominator for both transplant and mortality rates in each month.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 Step 4: Calculate Rates Per Million Population\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 In Excel, for each month:\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f3\fs26 \cf0 ODD_Liver_Transplant_Rate = (12-month-ending ODD liver transplant count / Mid-window population) \'d7 1,000,000\
ODD_Death_Rate = (12-month-ending predicted overdose deaths / Mid-window population) \'d7 1,000,000\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\fs24 \cf0 The output of these steps is the 
\f3\fs26 Mortality_Vs_Transplant.csv
\f1\fs24  file provided in the repository (same file used for Figure 2). The R code for first differencing, HAC regression, and plotting is provided separately.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
